{"id": "EUVD-2026-91382", "enisaUuid": "051cfce6-ecb2-3a01-b55d-7dab96314a05", "description": "Stack Overflow vulnerability in Apache Directory LDAP API.\n\n\n\nBefore binding, a client can send a deeply nested search filter that overflows the stack in the server's decoder.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Directory LDAP API: from 1.2.0 before 1.2.9.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 1.2.9, which fixes the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T09:48:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T21:07:19", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/fn3bwknn57266hx66w9vv6b4k8rfwcx7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-103552", "GHSA-mggr-349m-j697"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b370763-6210-3d73-b906-b501216de421", "product": {"name": "Apache Directory LDAP API", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "1.2.0 <1.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "14f0ff2f-1d1e-3474-a0db-0bd3a6e066dd", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}